Shelved experiment: GL texture-binding cache (not applied, never measured).

Drafted 2026-10-05 against 6462f42. Suppresses redundant glActiveTexture/glBindTexture
calls in port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp through a shadow of the actual GL bindings.

Shelved because:
- No timing evidence that redundant binds cost anything; gfx_pc.cpp already skips
  re-selecting unchanged textures (rendering_state.textures), and the replay and
  scope paths already dedupe with their own replayTex state.
- Unsafe as written: code outside gfx_opengl.cpp changes texture bindings mid-frame
  without invalidating the shadow (vr_hub_render binds 0 on units 0-3 after the eye
  passes; see vr_hub.cpp), so a later skipped bind would draw with the wrong texture.
- The replay test fixture only stubbed the wrappers as passthroughs, so the cache
  itself was never tested.

Revisit only if profiling attributes measurable time to texture binds. Apply with
  git apply docs/experiments/texture-binding-cache.patch
then make every external GL texture binder invalidate the shadow and add real tests.

